      meaning:
        "Following that perverse vision, a few debased men embraced — though others rejected — this heretic doctrine (pāṣaṇḍa-vāda): 'I am Brahman', 'I am attributeless', 'this world is unreal'. O Pavana (Vāyu)! Victorious is your third avatāra (Madhva) — a fire wreathed in garlands of flame, its pramāṇas (means of true knowledge) expert at burning down the spreading poison-tree of that web of specious reasoning (yukty-ābhāsa). — Śrī Hari and Vāyudeva, Maṇimanta's writings — claiming 'I am Brahman' and that everything is illusion — confounded the righteous; those poisonous works were destroyed by you in the avatāras of Sage Veda Vyāsa and Śrī Madhvācārya. We pay our obeisance to you. (Phala-śruti: this śloka gives success in debates.)"
